# Bali in Bengaluru — project rules for AI assistants

**Read `HANDOVER.md` in the repo root first** — it is the complete brief. This file
is the quick-reference version.

## What this is
A campaign hub website for the "Bali in Bengaluru" cultural festival by Param
Foundation. Plain **HTML + CSS + vanilla JS**, no framework, no build step, no
dependencies. Hosted on GitHub Pages (auto-deploys on push to `main`).
Live: https://p-cult.github.io/bali-in-blr/

## File map
- `index.html` — content & structure (sections marked with HTML comments; each has an `id`)
- `styles.css` — all styling; **design tokens are in `:root` at the top**; responsive `@media` at the bottom
- `main.js` — behaviour + the `CONFIG` data-bridge object at the very top
- `data/events.json`, `data/partners.json` — local stand-ins for Google Sheets
- `docs/BRIDGE-SETUP.md`, `docs/apps-script/Code.gs` — the backend bridge (not yet connected)

## Architecture
Data comes from **Google Sheets via a Google Apps Script Web App** ("the bridge").
Currently the calendar/partners read local JSON and the signup form is in demo mode.
To go live, set `CONFIG.BRIDGE_URL` and repoint `EVENTS_URL`/`PARTNERS_URL` in
`main.js` — no other changes. See HANDOVER §3–4.

## Rules
- Keep it **dependency-free** vanilla JS/CSS. Do not add frameworks, build tools, or
  npm packages without a strong, stated reason.
- Styling goes in `styles.css` using classes + `:root` tokens. No inline styles.
- Content edits go in `index.html`; data-driven content goes in `data/*.json` (later the Sheet).
- Always `esc()` any sheet/user-supplied value before inserting into HTML (XSS).
- **Privacy/compliance (Param Foundation):** personal data (emails/phones) may live
  only in approved systems (Google Workspace / Zoho). Never store PII in the repo,
  never send it to unapproved third parties, never expose personal rows on the public
  page — aggregates only. Keep the signup consent checkbox and purpose text (DPDP Act 2023).
- Prefer the Google + Zoho stack for any new integrations.
- Conventions: dates `DD MMM YYYY`, currency INR (₹), Indian English. Festival title
  is exactly "Bali in Bengaluru".
- After changing CSS/JS, bump the `?v=` query on their `<link>`/`<script>` tags in
  `index.html` for cache-busting.
- Run locally with a server (`python3 -m http.server 8000`), not `file://`, because
  the page `fetch()`es `data/*.json`.
